WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.440
Four careful censuses of mouse retinal ganglion cells gave at least 32, at least 35,

2
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.820
42, and 46. Each was done well.

3
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.640
Two are lower bounds, and they differ.

4
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.860
Ganglion cell axons form the optic nerve.

5
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.740
So how many kinds are there, and who is right?

6
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.340
Imaging counted cells by their light responses.

7
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:33.220
In isolated mouse retina, two photon imaging built a dataset of 11 ,210 cells.

8
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.000
But that layer also holds displaced amacrine cells.

9
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.560
Fourteen groups of them were set aside.

10
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.620
What remained was a minimum of 32 types.

11
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.780
The authors thought unusually abundant types probably hide further subdivisions.

12
00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:52.163
Sequencing counted cells by which genes they express.

13
00:00:52.803 --> 00:01:00.803
In adult mice, 35 ,699 ganglion cell transcriptomes fell into 45 clusters.

14
00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:04.583
Splitting one cluster into two known types gave 46.

15
00:01:05.303 --> 00:01:07.603
So clustering had missed a known difference.

16
00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:11.723
The smallest type was 0 .15 % of the cells.

17
00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:14.203
That is about 54 cells.

18
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:20.147
Recording from the same cell ties response, shape, and RNA to that one cell.

19
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:24.187
In some cells, the shape or the RNA was collected too.

20
00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:32.147
In isolated mouse retina, 1 ,859 ganglion cells were recorded and sorted into 42

21
00:01:32.147 --> 00:01:37.247
functional types. These matched an estimated 89% % of types in the anatomical

22
00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:41.527
catalogue. But the map to RNA was not always one to one.

23
00:01:41.527 --> 00:01:47.067
Three sustained O -N direction selective types aligned with a single cluster, called

24
00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.067
C10.

25
00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:50.897
Electron microscopy counted by shape.

26
00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:56.977
In one mouse retinal patch, the reconstructed cells formed 47 anatomical clusters.

27
00:01:57.557 --> 00:02:00.157
The supported lower bound was 35 types.

28
00:02:00.657 --> 00:02:02.077
47 counts clusters.

29
00:02:02.677 --> 00:02:04.717
35 is the number they could support.

30
00:02:05.197 --> 00:02:08.677
So the four numbers are not rival answers to one question.

31
00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:12.477
Each reflects a method, a preparation, and a resolution.

32
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.660
So when does a cluster become a type?

33
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.080
When response, shape, and expression are tied to one another.

34
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.300
The usual standard also asks for a mosaic.

35
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.080
Cells of the type space their bodies evenly; dendrites can overlap.

36
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.020
Ideally, genetic access agrees too.

37
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.500
The most trustworthy types are the ones that more than one method finds.

38
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.420
Ask what a number counted.
